  realLife: [
    { tag: 'INTEGRITY', tagZh: '正直', verseRef: 'Proverbs 28:1',
      titleZh: '不必再怕被发现', titleEn: 'No longer afraid of being found out',
      bodyZh: '“恶人虽无人追赶也逃跑；义人却胆壮像狮子”（28:1）。做了亏心事的人，即使没人知道，心里也总在“逃”——怕某封邮件被翻出来，怕某句谎话被戳穿。正直最实在的好处，就是这种坦然：你可以直视别人的眼睛，不必编故事，不必提防。若心里有一处正让你无法坦然，那也许正是神在邀请你回到光中。',
      bodyEn: 'The wicked flee when no one pursues, but the righteous are as bold as a lion (28:1). Someone who has done wrong keeps “running” inside even when no one knows — afraid an email will surface, a lie will be exposed. Integrity’s most concrete benefit is this ease: you can look people in the eye without inventing stories or staying on guard. If something is keeping you from that ease, it may be God’s invitation back into the light.' },
    { tag: 'CONFESSION', tagZh: '认罪', verseRef: 'Proverbs 28:13',
      titleZh: '遮掩，还是承认？', titleEn: 'Cover it up, or come clean?',
      bodyZh: '“遮掩自己罪过的，必不亨通；承认离弃罪过的，必蒙怜恤”（28:13）。我们的本能是掩盖——怕丢脸、怕后果。但遮掩会让人越来越枯干、越来越孤立。圣经指出一条相反的路：把它说出来，在神面前、也在合适的人面前诚实承认，并且真的转身离开。神迎接的不是完美的人，而是诚实的人。认罪不是自我惩罚，而是通往怜恤与自由的门。',
      bodyEn: 'He who conceals his sins doesn’t prosper, but whoever confesses and renounces them finds mercy (28:13). Our instinct is to cover up — afraid of shame, afraid of consequences. But hiding leaves us drier and more isolated. Scripture points to the opposite road: name it, honestly, before God and the right person, and actually turn from it. God welcomes not perfect people but honest ones. Confession isn’t self-punishment; it’s the doorway to mercy and freedom.' },
    { tag: 'MONEY & STEWARDSHIP', tagZh: '金钱与管理', verseRef: 'Proverbs 28:20',
      titleZh: '“快速致富”的诱惑', titleEn: 'The lure of getting rich quick',
      bodyZh: '“想要急速发财的，不免受罚”（28:20）。箴言并不反对努力工作带来的财富，它警告的是那颗“急速”的心——为了快点发财，愿意走捷径、冒不该冒的险、甚至牺牲诚实。今天的各种“稳赚不赔”“一夜翻倍”，往往正踩在这条线上。智慧的问题不是“我能赚多少”，而是“这条路诚实吗？我承受得起它的代价吗？”',
      bodyEn: 'One who is eager to be rich will not go unpunished (28:20). Proverbs isn’t against wealth earned through honest work; it warns about the hungry heart behind “quick” — willing to cut corners, take reckless risks, even trade away honesty to get there faster. Today’s “guaranteed returns” and “double your money overnight” schemes usually sit right on that line. The wise question isn’t “how much can I make?” but “is this path honest, and can I bear its cost?”' },
    { tag: 'GENEROSITY', tagZh: '慷慨', verseRef: 'Proverbs 28:27',
      titleZh: '不要装作看不见', titleEn: 'Don’t look away',
      bodyZh: '“周济贫穷的，不致缺乏；佯为不见的，必多受咒诅”（28:27）。这里提到一个很真实的动作——“装作看不见”。面对需要，我们常常不是拒绝，而是把目光移开，假装没注意到。慷慨的第一步，往往只是愿意真正“看见”。不必等到富有才开始给予；慷慨是一种信靠神供应的生活方式，而神应许，这样的人不致缺乏。',
      bodyEn: 'One who gives to the poor has no lack; but one who closes his eyes will have many curses (28:27). Notice the very real gesture here — “closing the eyes.” Faced with need, we often don’t so much refuse as look away and pretend not to notice. The first step of generosity is usually just being willing to truly see. You don’t have to wait until you’re wealthy to start giving; generosity is a way of life that trusts God’s supply — and he promises such a person will not lack.' },
    { tag: 'LEADERSHIP', tagZh: '领导', verseRef: 'Proverbs 28:12',
      titleZh: '掌权者的品格影响众人', titleEn: 'A leader’s character shapes everyone',
      bodyZh: '“义人得志，有大荣耀；恶人兴起，人就躲藏”（28:12）。这一章不断提醒：掌权者的正直不是私事。公义的领袖让人安心、让群体兴旺；贪婪、暴虐的当权者却让人叹息、躲藏（28:15–16、28）。无论你带领的是一个团队、一个家庭，还是一间教会，你的品格都在悄悄塑造身边人的安全感。以正直带领，本身就是对他人的祝福。',
      bodyEn: 'When the righteous triumph, there is great glory; but when the wicked rise, men hide themselves (28:12). This chapter keeps insisting that a leader’s integrity is not a private matter. Just leaders make people feel safe and let a community flourish; greedy, tyrannical rulers make people groan and hide (28:15–16, 28). Whether you lead a team, a family, or a church, your character quietly shapes the sense of safety around you. To lead with integrity is itself a blessing to others.' },
  ],

